# Degree ψ(N) of the level-N modular function field over K(j)

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqModC_modularFunctionFieldFullC_eq_dedekindPsi`
(`6a282126-81a4-505f-be2c-02fc1516c73b`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `ffa4c8f1-0aa0-5c2a-90d8-8332a484e2c9`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $K$ be a field and $N\ge 1$ a natural number whose image in $K$ is nonzero. Inside the field of
formal Laurent series $K((q))$ consider the element `jqModC K`, namely $q^{-1}$ times the
coefficientwise image in $K$ of the integral power series `jNum` $=E_4^3\cdot$ `dedekindEtaUnitInv`;
this is the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$ read in $K$. Let `modularFunctionFieldFullC K
N` be the intermediate field of $K((q))/K$ generated over $K$ by the set `divisorExpansionsC K N` of
all substitutions $q\mapsto q^{d}$ (written `qExpand K d`) applied to `jqModC K`, as $d$ runs over
the nonzero divisors of $N$; the case $d=1$ shows `jqModC K` itself lies in this field. The
assertion is that the $K$-subfield of `modularFunctionFieldFullC K N` generated by this single
element `jqModC K` has the whole of `modularFunctionFieldFullC K N` as an extension of finite rank
exactly `dedekindPsi N` $=\sum_{d\mid N,\ d\ \text{squarefree}} N/d = N\prod_{p\mid N}(1+1/p)$.
Since this value is positive, the extension is in particular finite.

This is the statement that the level-$N$ modular function field over a field $K$ in which $N$ is
invertible has degree $\psi(N)=[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}):\pm\Gamma_0(N)]$ over $K(j)$, the
positive-characteristic case being Igusa's theorem on the good reduction of the modular
correspondence. It underlies the construction and study of models of $X_0(N)$ over $K$ and of their
function fields, and is invoked throughout the treatment of mod $p$ modular forms and of fibres of
these models.

